    title: "A real app instead of a report",
    sentence: "Individual users struggled most with the Data Studio report, so in May 2026 I decided to build a real app with Claude Code. I'm proud of how it turned out, how quickly I built it, and how much better it is for users today.",
    full: "<p>Individual users had the most trouble with Data Studio and its poor UX. It wasn't intuitive: they couldn't easily find their data or analyse what was in it, and it was slow to load. After updating their data, or after their first entry, it took at least five minutes for any data to show up, and Data Studio could also lock data freshness to twelve hours, so it wouldn't show new data any sooner. None of that was good for users.</p><p>So in May 2026 I decided to try building a real app for individual users, using Claude Code. I started on 18 May, launched it on 24 June, and shut down the old report on 15 July.</p><p>I'm proud of how the app turned out, how quickly I built it, and how much better it is for users today.</p>",
